{
  "schema": "flint.repos/1",
  "note": "Repo split (plan section 7, ADR-030 section 2): every flint:* package belongs to one repo. Integrated repos (security, the data family, batch) sit between boot and framework, so boot -> integrated -> framework -> flint, and depend on each other only in Spring's own direction (data-* and security -> data-commons). Boot-based repos (ai, the cloud family, later shell) ship their own auto-configuration and depend on boot.",
  "layout_note": "Where a monorepo directory sits in its extracted repo, mirroring Spring's repos: engines under engine/<name>; Spring-layer modules (framework/<artifact>) at the top as flint-<artifact>, like spring-framework's spring-<module>; Boot in spring-boot's core/, module/, platform/ and starter/, where boot/core, boot/module, boot/platform and boot/starter keep their place and the pre-port Boot libraries and starters (boot/boot, boot/autoconfigure-*, boot/actuator, starters/*) move to legacy/, so they never collide with the Spring Boot packages of the same artifact names; the repo's API mapping (api/<repo>) becomes api/, and its native project (native/<repo>) native/. Each rule rewrites a directory's first two path components; a rule ending in / or - is a prefix, any other must match whole. The first match wins; the flint repo keeps the monorepo layout.",
  "layout": [
    ["packages/engine-", "engine/"],
    ["framework/", "flint-"],
    ["security/", "flint-"],
    ["boot/core", "core"],
    ["boot/module", "module"],
    ["boot/platform", "platform"],
    ["boot/starter", "starter"],
    ["boot/boot", "legacy/flint-boot"],
    ["boot/autoconfigure-", "legacy/flint-boot-autoconfigure-"],
    ["boot/actuator", "legacy/flint-boot-actuator"],
    ["boot/", "module/flint-boot-"],
    ["starters/starter", "legacy/flint-boot-starter"],
    ["starters/", "legacy/flint-boot-starter-"]
  ],
  "lock_partitions_note": "Inputs of policy/lock-partitions.json besides the locks (tools/platform_modules.py, flint check structural): shim_providers are the native libraries a repo's own Flint C shim archive wraps, which it carries even where other repos' packages consume them too (flint_ffi_base wraps libyaml and utf8proc); tool_consumers map a lock consumer that is a package's build tool to that package.",
  "lock_partitions": {
    "shim_providers": {"flint": ["libyaml", "utf8proc"]},
    "tool_consumers": {"rpc-codegen-build-tool": "engine-rpc"}
  },
